{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZtEJ2z7mr2jMeWijzx9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate `tally_drift_ideal`, and it passes the self-check with `OK`. Two warnings came with it that the full admission fit will have to settle:\n\n- **Loo reliability:** 4.6% of trials (119 of 2560) had Pareto k above 0.5, and the tolerance is 1%. On this short one-chain fit, PSIS-LOO counts as unreliable.\n- **Convergence:** it wasn't checked, because a single chain can't report R-hat.\n\nThe smoke fit's ELPD-LOO was −1117.6, well behind the incumbent's −973.3. The smoke fit used only 100 draws, so the gap may shrink in the full fit.\n\n**Hypothesis:** People keep a running tally of heads minus tails as they read a sequence. They judge it random when the tally wanders away from balance by about as much as they expect a fair coin's tally to wander. The whole path counts, not just the final count. A streak that drives the tally far from balance counts against a sequence even if it later corrects. A tally that never leaves balance also counts against it. Each person has their own ideal amount of wandering.\n\n**How the model works:** The drift measure is the average squared running lead, divided by what a fair coin would give for that length, on a log scale. Each participant's ideal drift comes from a population distribution, parameterised non-centred. Each sequence scores minus its squared distance from the person's ideal. The choice is a sigmoid of the score difference, scaled by one shared sensitivity parameter.\n\n**Why it's different:** The critique's one discrepancy that survives FDR is that people avoid long streaks more than alternation rate predicts. This model addresses it through a different mechanism from the existing ones. `max_lopsided_stretch_ideal` uses only the single worst stretch, and `ideal_alternation_with_balance` uses only the final H/T count. Here streaks, overall imbalance and rigid alternation are all judged through one path statistic. Novelty against the other models isn't tested by the self-check.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_0`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2587,"cache_read_input_tokens":53628,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2587,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b95be6b-d30d-4729-8146-12fafacdb50b","uuid":"1fd0f024-55ee-405f-b98d-86a3b7aa4f52","timestamp":"2026-09-30T15:46:32.490Z","request_id":"req_011CfZtEGzE1Qj22ikkY7dES"}
